      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—that exhaustion is real, and it makes sense that you feel stuck when effort doesn't seem to shift anything. Sometimes the most important step isn't trying harder, but pausing to ask what you actually need right now, even if it's just rest. You don't have to solve everything at once; maybe just name one tiny thing that feels less heavy today. And if you're open to it, talking to a therapist or counselor could help you see patterns you can't from inside the treadmill.",
